+//
+// jk2coop: co-op player helpers (g_utils.cpp)
+//
+// Single-player code says "the player" as `ent->s.number == 0` (or
+// `!ent->s.number`). In co-op every human gets its own slot in
+// [0, MAX_CLIENTS) - the host is 0, joiners are 1..3 - and NPCs always live at
+// >= MAX_CLIENTS, so those checks quietly treat every joiner as an NPC (weaker
+// shots, no item pickups, no damage protection, ...). G_IsCoopPlayer is the
+// slot-independent replacement: true for the host AND every joiner, false for
+// every NPC. Identical to the old check in plain single player.
